1
00:00:03,370 --> 00:00:06,325
The Receive inbox has to read every stealth announcement

2
00:00:06,365 --> 00:00:09,146
since launch and test each one against the viewing key,

3
00:00:09,186 --> 00:00:14,011
locally. Monad's RPC returns logs 100 blocks at a time,

4
00:00:14,051 --> 00:00:16,522
so the first version took many minutes.

5
00:00:16,758 --> 00:00:20,271
Now the history comes from Envio HyperSync in one query,

6
00:00:20,311 --> 00:00:23,327
and only the newest blocks are read over RPC.

7
00:00:23,538 --> 00:00:27,403
Scan, and the inbox is ready in about two seconds.

8
00:00:27,635 --> 00:00:30,083
It finds all three payments from the demo:

9
00:00:30,166 --> 00:00:34,735
an encrypted 0.3 cUSDC that my stealth key reveals,

10
00:00:34,775 --> 00:00:40,807
the 0.44955 USDC private bridge delivery on Sepolia,

11
00:00:40,847 --> 00:00:43,875
and the 0.01 MON stealth send.

12
00:00:44,358 --> 00:00:46,570
This is the raw route behind it:

13
00:00:46,610 --> 00:00:50,382
the announcer's logs, served from Envio HyperSync.

14
00:00:50,685 --> 00:00:53,118
The Envio token stays on the server,

15
00:00:53,158 --> 00:00:56,015
and matching happens only in the browser.

